! Introduction

<<.from-version "5.5.0">> The ''dialog'' widget displays its content as a modal dialog. While the dialog is displayed the rest of the page is inert: it cannot be clicked, focused or reached by assistive technology.

The dialog is displayed for as long as the widget is rendered. It is usually placed within a ListWidget or RevealWidget that determines when it appears.

! Content and Attributes

The content of the `<$dialog>` widget is displayed within the dialog.

|!Attribute |!Description |
|class |An optional CSS class name to be assigned to the HTML element |
|role |The ARIA role of the dialog: `dialog` (the default) or `alertdialog` |
|aria-* |Any attributes with the prefix `aria-` are assigned to the HTML element. Use `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby` to name the dialog |

The widget generates a `<div>` element with the attribute `aria-modal="true"`. When it is rendered:

* The `inert` attribute is assigned to the siblings of the element and to the siblings of each of its ancestors
* The focus moves to the first button, link or input control within the dialog

When the widget is removed the `inert` attributes are removed again and the focus returns to where it was.

The widget does not position its content. Styles are assigned through the `class` attribute.

